- test 5 (line 113): assertion at line 123: `legacyChanges.length >= 1 && legacyChanges.every(...)` — expected true, actual false. So no legacyCode deprecation found at path 'legacyCode'... OR affected empty. Line 123 col 29 is `assert.ok(perPolicyLegacy.affected.some(...))`? Let me count: test 5 starts at 113. Lines:

113: test('policy-api 1 -> 2: ...', () => {
114:   const res = analyse(...);
115:   assert.equal(res.verdict.status, 'PUBLISHED_OK');
116:   assert.equal(res.counts.DANGEROUS, 0);
117:   assert.equal(res.counts.WARNING, 0);
118:   assert.equal(res.counts.DEPRECATED, 4, ...);
119:
120:   const legacyChanges = res.changes.filter((c) => c.path === 'legacyCode');
121:   assert.ok(legacyChanges.length >= 1 && legacyChanges.every((c) => c.severity === 'DEPRECATED'));
122:   const perPolicyLegacy = legacyChanges.find((c) => c.endpointKey === 'GET /policies/{policyId}');
123:   assert.ok(perPolicyLegacy.affected.some((a) => a.consumer === 'payments-svc'), 'payments-svc reads legacyCode');

So legacyChange found (line 121 passed) but affected doesn't include payments-svc. Why? The consumer payments-svc reads 'legacyCode' — the deprecation change path is 'legacyCode' — matchFieldChange: reqSide = false (direction response) → declared = reads = ['policyId','status','premiumDue.amount','premiumDue.dueDate','legacyCode'] → hits = pool.filter(s => sameOrAncestor(s, changedPath) || sameOrAncestor(changedPath, s)) — 'legacyCode' === 'legacyCode' → hit. So affected should include payments-svc IF targetUsages includes payments-svc's usage GET /policies/{policyId}. change.endpointKey = 'GET /policies/{policyId}' — wait! The endpoint key in the flat model is `${method} ${normalizePath(path)}` = 'GET /policies/{}'. normalizePath replaces {policyId} → {}. So endpointKey is 'GET /policies/{}' not 'GET /policies/{policyId}'!! But the debug output earlier showed '@ GET /policies/{policyId}' — because change.endpoint (the label) uses the RAW path, while endpointKey uses normalized. In my test I used endpointKey === 'GET /policies/{policyId}' — wrong; should be 'GET /policies/{}'.

Same issue in test 6 (line 138): legacyChanges.find(endpointKey === 'GET /policies/{policyId}') → undefined → reading .affected of undefined → error. Fix to 'GET /policies/{}'.

Test 10 (line 188): `getChange = reqChanges.find(c => c.endpointKey === 'GET /claims/{claimId}')` → should be 'GET /claims/{}'. Same fix.

Also quote tests used 'POST /quotes' (no params) — fine.

Let me fix these three.

